{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NTEzMTIy","is_bot":false,"login":"tobias-tengler","name":"Tobias Tengler"},"baseRefOid":"9a563e814f3b6213c80a6bc96a01fbcb4d605096","body":"Tiny JSON-lines data tables and their metadata tables share the same sixteen-entry pool bucket. Large lookup batches exhaust that bucket and keep allocating oversized tables on warm requests.\n\nThis PR adds pool buckets of lengths 1, 2, 4 and 8 so tiny data tables no longer consume the sixteen-entry metadata bucket.\n\n### Benchmarks\n\nEach direct operation creates the real arena, rents a data table of minimum length 1 and a metadata table of minimum length 9 per record, then seals and disposes the arena. Tracker growth and returns are timed; JSON parsing is excluded.\n\nBenchmarkDotNet 0.15.8, Release .NET 10.0.12 ARM64, server/concurrent GC: three launches, five warmup iterations and fifteen measured iterations per launch. Values are medians after BDN outlier filtering; ratios are relative to the baseline. Baseline `main` is `9a563e814f`; the PR is `c60ca7b2ae`.\n\nBoth variants use `DOTNET_GCDynamicAdaptationMode=0` for microbenchmarks and HTTP comparisons to avoid observed allocation-counter discontinuities. This is a measurement setting, not a production change; default-GC HTTP CPU/allocation effects are not independently established.\n\n| Case | Version | Median | Ratio | Allocated | Alloc Ratio |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 2,048 records | `main` | 79.685 µs | 1.00 | 97,888 B | 1.00 |\n| 2,048 records | PR | 78.403 µs | 0.98 | 97,888 B | 1.00 |\n| 5,000 records | `main` | 368.725 µs | 1.00 | 1,849,353 B | 1.00 |\n| 5,000 records | PR | 274.600 µs | 0.74 | 485,534 B | 0.26 |\n\nAt 2,048 records, timings overlap and allocations are unchanged. At 5,000 records, median time falls 25.53% and allocations fall 73.75%. The synthetic large case has more Gen0/1/2 collections despite allocating fewer bytes.\n\n### Verdict\n\nFor 5,000-entity HTTP lookups, allocation/request fell 42.09% in the primary runs and 38.12% in a fresh pair. No stable gateway CPU or throughput gain was established. The added buckets reserve about 128 KiB of slot arrays and can retain about 1.31 MiB of extra table objects when full. The fresh large pair had 2.36% higher p95 and 4.56% higher p99 latency; latency equivalence and a general RSS benefit remain unproven.\n\nRelease builds passed; 181 focused tests passed, with one existing skip. [Full results and reproduction](https://github.com/ChilliCream/graphql-platform/blob/c60ca7b2aeea89a1f54d09cdbbd91cfb8dea4708/PERFORMANCE-batch-metadata.md).\n","comments":[],"files":[{"path":"PERFORMANCE-batch-metadata.md","additions":149,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/Directory.Build.props","additions":10,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/README.md","additions":76,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/agg_speedscope.py","additions":57,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/analyze.py","additions":102,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/analyze_profiles.py","additions":31,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/audit.py","additions":84,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/campaign.py","additions":163,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/gateway/Gateway.csproj","additions":12,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/gateway/Program.cs","additions":29,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/gateway/appsettings.json","additions":1,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/lifecycle.py","additions":64,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/load.js","additions":38,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchma